# Exercise 2: Adding Text in Base R

## Part 1: Exploring `paste()` and `paste0()`

> **Question:** Use R Help to learn about the `paste()` function. Run examples to understand the difference between `paste()` and `paste0()`.

::: callout-note
The `paste()` function combines values with a space by default. The `paste0()` function combines them without adding a space.
:::

```{r}
#| label: exercise-2-part-1

# Open the help document
?paste

# paste() adds a space between the text and number
paste("Item", 1:3)

# paste0() joins them without a space
paste0("Item", 1:3)

# collapse combines multiple values into one text string
paste(1:5, collapse = ", ")
```

